{95}{The obvious choice seemed to be the half ogres. Tired of being hunted, and the promise of large amounts of food gained the gnomes extremely loyal bodyguards. But there was a problem. An half ogre was a very rare thing in those days, and with good scientifical reasons for being so. And the gnomes without bodyguards were used as leverage against those protected.}{The obvious choice seemed to be the half ogres. Tired of being hunted, and the promise of large amounts of food gained the gnomes extremely loyal bodyguards. But there was a problem. An half ogre was a very rare thing in those days, and with good scientifical reasons for being so. And the gnomes without bodyguards were used as leverage against those protected.}{}{}{}{}
